@startuml
title Figure 10 — UML Deployment diagram — runtime nodes and communication paths
top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 55

node "Operator device" as Device <<device>> {
  artifact "Web browser" as Browser
}

node "Docker Compose / Linux host" as Host <<executionEnvironment>> {
  node "frontend service / container" as Web <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "React operator UI" as React
  }

  node "API service / container" as Api <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "Spring Boot modular monolith" as Spring
    artifact "Offline adapters\nStaticPolicyAdapter +\nDeterministicAnalysisStub" as Offline
  }

  node "database service / container" as DB <<database>> {
    artifact "PostgreSQL + pgvector" as PostgreSQL
  }
}

node "External AI provider" as Provider <<external>>

Browser --> Web : HTTP\nlocal baseline
Web --> Api : HTTP/JSON /api/*\nCompose private network
Api --> DB : JDBC / PostgreSQL\nTCP 5432 private network
Api ..> Provider : HTTPS provider API\nonly when explicitly configured
Api --> Offline : in-process baseline path

note bottom of Host
  The mandatory baseline is local and does not require a reverse proxy.
  TLS termination, ingress, load balancing, or a reverse proxy are deployment-specific
  concerns and are intentionally not prescribed while AMB-DEP-001 remains unresolved.
  No WebSocket, broker, FIFO, Redis, or separate identity service is assumed.
end note
@enduml
